        {
          "id": "2019-08-14a",
          "kind": "portal_message",
          "start": "2019-08-14T16:20",
          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Patient Communication",
              "title": "Your lab results",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2019-08-14T16:20",
              "body": "Hi Julie,\n\nYour labs are back. Kidney function, sugar, thyroid and blood counts are normal. A1c is 5.6, top end of normal, worth watching with your brother's diabetes. Cholesterol is acceptable and doesn't need a medicine.\n\nLiver enzymes (AST and ALT) are mildly up, which is what we'd expect with active hepatitis C. Bilirubin and albumin are normal. The hepatitis C virus level is detectable, so the infection is still active. HIV screen negative. Hepatitis B: you've never had it, and you're not immune either, which is why the Twinrix series matters. See you in about a month for dose two.\n\nPCP"
            }
          ]
